  "goodToKnow": "Dergleichen means such things or the like, and never changes its form: und dergleichen (and the like, abbreviated u. dgl.), nichts dergleichen (nothing of the sort): Er tat nichts dergleichen. It's slightly formal; in speech, Germans say und so weiter or so was. Similar: desgleichen (likewise) and derlei (such): derlei Probleme. It's built from an old genitive: der gleichen (of the same kind)."
